Thanks for pulling this together, Charlie! A few thoughts:

On the infrastructure migration — I'd like to propose that we delay
the database stateful set migration by one week. The observability
team has identified a gap in our monitoring coverage for the new
Kubernetes cluster. We need at least another week to get proper
metrics and alerting in place before we move the databases.

Specifically, we're missing:

  * Disk IOPS metrics on the new CSI driver
  * Proper PDB and anti-affinity rules for the DB pods
  * Load testing results for the new storage class

Better to delay one week than to have an incident during migration.

On the Q3 OKRs — the 90% test coverage target is ambitious. Currently
we're at about 62% on critical paths. I've done some rough estimation
and I think we can hit 80% by end of Q3 with the current team size.
To get to 90% we'd likely need dedicated time from at least one more
engineer, or we need to reduce scope elsewhere.

I've attached a spreadsheet with the detailed breakdown per service.
Happy to discuss further in the retro.

For the "what slowed us down" discussion item — I think one big thing
was context switching. We had 4 different incidents last quarter that
required 3+ engineers to drop everything for an entire day. The new
on-call rotation should help, but I wonder if we should also invest
in better runbooks and automated remediation.

See you all at 2 PM!

Alice

